#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting the Properties for a Frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: formatframes.docbook:12 formatframes.docbook:87 formatframes.docbook:88
#: formatframes.docbook:170 formatframes.docbook:236 formatframes.docbook:261
#: formatframes.docbook:262 formatframes.docbook:263 formatframes.docbook:310
#: formatframes.docbook:327 formatframes.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "frames"
msgstr "imatges"

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "configure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "For each frame in your document, you can determine:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "how &kword; handles full text frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "how text wraps around or through overlapping frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "the exact size of the frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "establish margins within a frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "set a background color and pattern for the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All of these options can be altered using a set of dialog boxes, or by using "
"a previously defined <emphasis>framestyle</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <emphasis>framestyle</emphasis> is a predefined set of frameset formatting "
"options which is given a name. Once a frameset has been assigned a "
"framestyle, any changes made to the framestyle will be reflected in all "
"framesets which are assigned that framestyle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may be noticing that framestyles function in a way similar to "
"<emphasis>text styles</emphasis>. The main difference, is framestyles "
"control the look of the frame, and textstyles control the look of paragraphs "
"within the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the frame settings dialogs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All of these settings can be determined in the <guilabel>Frame Properties</"
"guilabel> dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to adjust the properties of any frame, you must first select the "
"frame you want to change."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply click once on the frame border of the frame you want to edit. (Or by "
"holding down the &Ctrl; key and clicking inside the frame with the &LMB;.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You edit the properties of a frameset using a set of dialogs which you can "
"open one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame/Frameset "
"Properties</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse pointer on the border of the frame, and click once with the "
"&RMB;. A small menu will appear. Select <guimenuitem>Frame/Frameset "
"Properties...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Properties dialog consists of one dialog box, with six index tabs "
"labeled <link linkend=\"format-frame-options\">Options</link>, <link linkend="
"\"format-frame-tra\">Text Run Around</link>, <link linkend=\"format-frame-"
"connect\">Connect Text Frames</link>, <link linkend=\"format-frame-geometry"
"\">Geometry</link>, <link linkend=\"format-frame-background\">Background</"
"link> and <link linkend=\"format-frame-borders\">Borders</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Options"
msgstr "Opcions generalas"

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "configure automatic creation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "protect contents of"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tab labeled <guilabel>Options</guilabel> is used to determine how "
"&kword; behaves when there is too much text to fit within the current bounds "
"of the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; has three solutions to this situation:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a frame becomes full, &kword; automatically creates a new page. On this "
"new page, it may create a new frame, of the same size and position, if you "
"choose."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resize last frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a frame becomes full, &kword; automatically extends the bottom border "
"of the text frame to accommodate the new text. It will continue to expand as "
"new text is added. Conversely, it will shrink again if text is removed from "
"the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Don't show the extra text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does not create a new frame or change the current frame in any way. "
"You will need to manually resize the current frame, or add a new frame to "
"the frame set."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply make your selection in the section labeled <guilabel>If Text is Too "
"Long for Frame</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the section entitled <guilabel>On New Page Creation</guilabel>, you have "
"three options available. You must select one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reconnect frame to current flow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a new frame, the same size and shape on a new page, and make it the "
"last frame in the frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do not create a followup frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creates a new page, but not a new frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Place a copy of this frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Creates a new page, with a new frame the same size, shape and position on "
"the page. Additionally, &kword; copies the contents of the frame from the "
"previous page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is useful for title frames, headers and footer frames. Each page will "
"have an automatic copy of this information on any new pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in the check box labeled <guilabel>Changes will be "
"applied to all frames in frameset</guilabel>, then any changes made in the "
"frame properties dialog box will automatically be applied to all frames "
"within the frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in the check box labeled <guilabel>Protect content</"
"guilabel>, &kword; will not allow any changes to the text within the frame, "
"or the formatting of the text within the frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can still reshape or even delete the frame, but the content within the "
"frame is locked. To lock the location and size of the frame, see the <link "
"linkend=\"format-frame-geometry\">Geometry</link> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make changes to the text, you need to remove the mark from "
"<guilabel>Protect content</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Flow around frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "force text around"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To adjust how text flows around overlapping frames, click the tab labeled "
"<guilabel>Text Run Around</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you overlay two text frames, and text from both frames is competing for "
"the same space on the page, &kword; can (at your option), make sure that "
"text from two frames does not overlap."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you can see from the options in the dialog box, there are three possible "
"choices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text will run through this frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting this option, &kword; will ignore this frame when it displays "
"the text in overlapping frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text will run around the frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting this option, &kword; will wrap the text of overlapping frames "
"around this frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, you can determine which side the text runs "
"around in the section labeled <guilabel>Run Around Side</guilabel>. Simply "
"choose <guilabel>Left</guilabel>, <guilabel>Right</guilabel>, or "
"<guilabel>Longest side</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatframes.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text will not run around this frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting this option, &kword; will not wrap any text around the edges of "
"this frame, but instead, will skip down below this frame before continuing "
"to display text in overlapping frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also determine how close your frames appear by setting the "
"<guilabel>Distance Between Frame &amp; Text</guilabel> in the spin boxes "
"provided. If you place a mark in the checkbox labeled <guilabel>Synchronize "
"changes</guilabel> &kword; will make all distances equal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move a frame to a new frameset"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "edit framesets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: formatframes.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "framesets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "edit"
msgstr "edicion"

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change which frameset the current frame belongs to by selecting the "
"<guilabel>Connect Text Frames</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog gives you the option to create a new frameset for the current "
"frame or move the selected frame to a current frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>Select existing frameset to connect frame to:</guilabel>, "
"to add the current frame to a previously created frameset. Choose one of the "
"framesets listed in the table below to specify which frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new frameset, select <guilabel>Create a new frameset:</guilabel> "
"and type the name of the new frameset in the text box labeled <guilabel>Name "
"of frameset</guilabel>. &kword; will create a new frameset with the current "
"frame as the only frame in the frameset (for now)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is helpful to name your framesets with descriptive names. Name the "
"frameset with a description of the contents so that you can quickly refer to "
"it again later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frame size and position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "geometry"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "determine size (dialog box)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "determine position (dialog box)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can adjust the size and position of your frame by clicking on the tab "
"labeled <guilabel>Geometry</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog box allows you to specify <emphasis>exactly</emphasis> where the "
"frame goes and how large it is."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you put a mark in the check box labeled <guilabel>Protect size and "
"position</guilabel>, the frame size and position will be fixed at their "
"current location. You will not be able to move the frame on the page until "
"this box is unchecked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "Determine Size and Position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can locate your frame on the page by first entering the <guilabel>Left:</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Top:</guilabel> measurements. This determines where "
"the top left corner of the frame will be. All measurements are from the top "
"left corner of the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also determine the exact size of the frame by entering its "
"<guilabel>Height:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Width:</guilabel> in the text "
"boxes provided. These two measurements are relative to the top left corner "
"of the frame you specified above. not to the size of the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "Determine Margins in the Frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the boxes labeled <guilabel>Left:</guilabel>, <guilabel>Right:</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>Top:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Bottom:</guilabel>, you "
"can establish margins <emphasis>within the frame</emphasis>. This should not "
"be confused with margins for the page, which are defined in the <link "
"linkend=\"page-format\">page properties dialog box</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guilabel>Synchronize changes</guilabel> check box has a mark in it, "
"&kword; will take any changes you make to one margin, and automatically "
"apply them to the other 3 margins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In other words, if this check box is selected, and you enter a margin of 1 "
"cm in any of the 4 margin boxes, all 4 frame margins will now become 1 cm in "
"size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "If this option is off, each text box can be given a different value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frame Background"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "background colors and patterns"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can adjust the background color of the text frame by selecting the "
"<guilabel>Background</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the color of the background by clicking on the button labeled "
"<guibutton>Background color:</guibutton>. The color is selected using the "
"<link linkend=\"select-colors\">Color selection dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frame Borders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "borders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the borders of the text frame by selecting the "
"<guilabel>Borders</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the <guilabel>Style:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Width:</guilabel> of "
"the borders with the two drop down boxes on the left side of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the color of the borders by clicking on the button labeled "
"<guibutton>Color:</guibutton>. The color is selected using the <link linkend="
"\"select-colors\">Color selection dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the four icons (<guiicon>Border Left</guiicon>, <guiicon>Border Right</"
"guiicon>, <guiicon>Border Top</guiicon> and <guiicon>Border Bottom</"
"guiicon>) below the <guibutton>Color</guibutton> button to determine on "
"which side of the frame you want to have a border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guilabel>Preview</guilabel> of the selected settings is shown on the "
"right side of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to accept all of your changes and to close "
"the dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> to accept all of your changes without "
"closing the dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to forget all of your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using frame styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "frame styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: formatframes.docbook:358 formatframes.docbook:362 formatframes.docbook:374
#: formatframes.docbook:406 formatframes.docbook:432 formatframes.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "frame style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "using"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting a frame with a framestyle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "apply frame style to a frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "To format a frame using a predefined framestyle simply:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the frame(s) by holding down &Ctrl; and clicking within the frame "
"with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guisubmenu>Framestyle</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice> from the menubar. A submenu will appear, listing "
"all the currently defined framestyles. Select the name of the framestyle you "
"want and all selected frames will automatically be formatting using the "
"options of that framestyle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing a framestyle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the options of a framestyle, you will need to use the framestyle "
"manager."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Style "
"Manager...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All of the currently defined framestyles are listed in the listbox on the "
"left. The currently selected framestyle is highlighted, and the name of the "
"currently selected framestyle is listed in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Name</guilabel>. (In this example, the currently selected "
"framestyle is <emphasis>Light Gray</emphasis>.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the framestyle you want to change by clicking on the name of the "
"framestyle in the listbox on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three tabs in on the right side of the dialog box: "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel>, <guilabel>Borders</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Background</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab, you can change the name of the "
"liststyle by typing the new name in the text box labeled <guilabel>Name</"
"guilabel>. You can also see a preview of what your frame will look like in "
"the preview box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Borders</guilabel> tab works the same as the tab of the same "
"name when formatting a paragraph. For more specific information click <link "
"linkend=\"para-borders\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Background</guilabel> tab operates identically to the same tab "
"when formatting a frame. Click <link linkend=\"format-frame-background"
"\">here</link> for more specific instructions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once all changes have been made, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save "
"your changes. All of the affected framesets will be changed to reflect the "
"new options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a new framestyle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "create new"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new framestyle, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Style Manager...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select a framestyle from the list at the left which most closely matches "
"your new desired framestyle by clicking on the name with the &LMB;. The "
"selected framestyle will be used as a template for the new framestyle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button. &kword; will generate a new "
"framestyle, which is a copy of the previously selected framestyle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose a name for your new framestyle, and type it in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Name</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now change your frame border and background options. For details, "
"see <link linkend=\"framestyle-edit\">Editing a framestyle</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are finished creating your framestyle, click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>, and your framestyle is saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Framestyles are specific for each document. A framestyle created in one "
"document can not be used in another document unless you <link linkend="
"\"framestyle-import\">import the framestyle</link> from that document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a framestyle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete framestyle, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Frames</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Style Manager...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the framestyle you want to delete by clicking once with the &LMB; in "
"the list on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will not allow you to delete the <emphasis>Plain</emphasis> "
"framestyle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the order of the framestyles in the list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the order that the framestyles are listed, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Style Manager...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The order the framestyles are listed in the menu is determined by the order "
"of the framestyles in the list on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the framestyle you want to move from the list at the left by clicking "
"once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click on the up and down arrows located at the bottom of the list of "
"framestyles. This will move the selected framestyle up or down in the list "
"of framestyles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are satisfied with the order of the list, select <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatframes.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "Importing a framestyle from another &kword; file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatframes.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "importing from another file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To import a framestyle from another &kword; file, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Style Manager...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the button labeled <guibutton>Import From File...</guibutton> to open "
"the <link linkend=\"file-dialog\">file selection dialog</link>.   Choose "
"your file, and click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new dialog box will appear listing all available framestyles for importing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &kword; encounters a duplicate framestyle name in the selected file, it "
"will append a number to the end of the framestyle name to identify the "
"imported style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example, if you import the <emphasis>Plain</emphasis> framestyle from "
"another &kword; file, &kword; will change the name to <emphasis>Plain-1</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <emphasis>all</emphasis> the framestyles you want to import. Then "
"click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatframes.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The framestyles will now appear at the bottom of your list of framestyles. "
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save the framestyles to the new document."
msgstr ""
